The central design constraint is now clear: geometry and font metrics can tell us how many cells fit at a chosen font, but they cannot decide how much readability to trade for more cells without an explicit policy. I’m separating the default “preserve preference” rule from an optional, semantically named classic-layout mode so constants don’t sneak back in disguised as formulas.
